<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{headline}}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{description}}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Domain Hound">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{headline}}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{description}}">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://domainhound.dev/sf/share.png">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{description}}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://domainhound.dev/sf/">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://domainhound.dev/sf/">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/hound-mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/home.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/sf/page.css">
  <script type="module" src="/sf/page.mjs"></script>
  <script type="module" src="/sf/funding-table.mjs"></script>
</head>
<body>
<header><div class="frame mast">
  <a class="paper-art" href="/" aria-label="Domain Hound home">
    <span class="paper-word first">Domain</span><span class="paper-word second">Hound</span>
    <span class="paper-dog"><img src="/assets/hound-mark.svg" width="180" height="180" alt=""></span>
  </a>
  <a class="jump" href="#check">Check a name</a>
</div></header>
<main>
  <article>
  <header class="intro"><div class="frame spread">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">San Francisco Bay Area &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{month}}</p>
      <h1>{{headlineLead}}<br>{{headlineFollowup}}</h1>
      <p class="dek">{{dek}}</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="ticket" aria-label="Emergent funding postcard">
      <div class="ticket-top"><span>San Francisco</span><b>.sh</b></div>
      <strong>{{leadAmount}}</strong><p>raised by Emergent</p>
      <svg class="postcard-scene" viewBox="0 0 400 110" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <defs>
          <g id="gate-span" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <!-- The nearer tower and deck sit higher in the perspective view. -->
            <path d="M-4 77Q37 69 97 12Q167 112 279 44Q326 87 404 87" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <path d="M18 71v14m19-24v24m19-37v37m20-54v54m42-48v49m18-32v33m19-23v24m19-19v19m19-16v17m19-18v18m20-22v23m19-30v30m17-40v41m30-28v29m18-18v19m19-12v13m20-9v9m21-5v6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <path d="M-4 84l408 10" stroke-width="5"/>
            <path d="M90 101l3-94h3l-1 94zm12 0l-2-94h3l4 94zm171 0l3-63h2l-1 63zm9 0l-2-63h2l4 63z" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <path d="M94 14h7m-7 7h7m-8 16h9m-10 16h11m-11 17h12m172-26h6m-7 9h8m-8 12h8m-9 13h10" stroke-width="3"/>
          </g>
        </defs>
        <path fill="var(--mist)" d="M0 0h400v110H0z"/>
        <circle cx="331" cy="30" r="18" fill="var(--leaf)"/>
        <path fill="var(--mint)" d="M0 60q30-14 59-9t52 5q25-1 53-12t55-6q30 6 55 24t57 9q40-13 69-8v47H0z"/>
        <path fill="var(--paper)" d="M0 67h70q8 0 8 3t-8 3H0zm180-7h74q7 0 7 2.5t-7 2.5h-74q-6 0-6-2.5t6-2.5z"/>
        <use href="#gate-span"/>
        <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 76q16 0 34 9l32 17q8 4 17 8H0zm400 7q-23 0-44 10t-50 17h94z"/>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="ticket-foot"><b>emergent.sh</b><span>Summer 2024 batch</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div></header>
  <div class="bay-divider" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 104" focusable="false"><use href="#gate-span"/></svg></div>
  <div class="reading">
    <p class="lede">Emergent turns a written idea into a working app. Among the Bay Area startups we counted in Y Combinator’s directory, only {{shCount}} use its .sh ending.</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="picks-title">
      <h2 id="picks-title">{{picksTitle}}</h2>
      <ol id="picks">{{picks}}</ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="ten-title">
      <h2 id="ten-title">The top 10 go well beyond .com</h2>
      <p>{{tenNote}}</p>
      <table id="top-ten" aria-labelledby="ten-title"><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Ending</th><th>Sites</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{topTen}}</tbody></table>
    </section>
    <section class="ai-trend" aria-labelledby="ai-trend-title">
      <h2 id="ai-trend-title">{{trendTitle}}</h2>
      <p class="chart-note">In {{firstBatch}}, {{firstAi}}% used .ai. The share peaked at {{trendPeak}}. In {{latest}} it stood at {{trendLatest}}.</p>
      <figure aria-label="Share of sites using .ai by YC batch">
        <div class="trend-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>YC batch</span><span>.ai share</span><span>Batch size</span></div>
        <div class="trend-plot">{{trend}}</div>
      </figure>
      <details class="compare"><summary>Compare all endings by batch</summary>
        <p>Pick a bar or choose a batch to see the counts.</p>
    <div class="legend"><span><i class="com"></i>.com</span><span><i class="ai"></i>.ai</span><span><i class="io"></i>.io</span><span><i class="rest"></i>Other endings</span></div>
    <div class="plot">
      <div class="axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>100%</span><span>50%</span><span>0%</span></div>
      <div class="years">{{bars}}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="batch-readout"><select aria-label="YC batch" id="batch-select" disabled>{{options}}</select><span id="batch-summary" role="status">{{summary}}</span></div>
    <details class="batch-details"><summary>All endings in this batch</summary>
      <table><caption>{{latest}}</caption><thead><tr><th>Ending</th><th>Sites</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{tableRows}}</tbody></table>
    </details>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section id="funding" class="funding-band"><div class="frame">
    <h2>The 50 best-funded on our shortlist</h2>
    <p class="deck">We checked {{candidates}} Bay Area startups for public funding figures. The list covers large teams, companies with verified SEC filings and Emergent.</p>
    <p>Corgi tops the list at {{corgiAmount}}. Next come Emergent on .sh and HappyRobot on .ai. {{fundingHeadline}}</p>

    <div class="funding-tools">
      <label class="funding-picker" hidden>Sort by <select id="funding-sort"></select></label>
    </div>
    <table id="company-table" aria-label="Bay Area YC companies ranked by funding" aria-describedby="funding-source">
      <thead><tr>{{fundingHeaders}}</tr></thead><tbody>{{companyRows}}</tbody>
    </table>
    <button class="more-rows" id="more-companies" aria-controls="company-table" aria-expanded="false" type="button" hidden>Show all 50 companies</button>
    <p id="funding-source" class="funding-note">Publicly disclosed funding, including SEC filings. Checked {{fundingDay}}.</p>
  </div></section>
  <div class="reading">
  <section>
    <h2>{{different}} .com sites put a twist on the name</h2>
    <p>Among the {{comCount}} .com sites, {{different}} used something other than the company’s exact name before the dot. Across all endings, {{get}} startups put “get” in front of their name and {{try}} used “try”.</p>
    <p>The median name was {{median}} characters long before the dot. The shortest had {{shortest}} character and the longest had {{longest}}.</p>
    <details><summary>More naming facts and name shapes</summary>
      <p>We found {{distinct}} endings. {{single}} showed up once. Before the dot, {{hyphen}} names had a hyphen and {{digits}} had a digit.</p>
      <h3>How the brand names read</h3>
      <p>We sorted names by spelling. An English dictionary can miss surnames and words in other languages.</p>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Name shape</th><th>Brands</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{shapes}}</tbody></table>
    </details>
  </section>
  <!-- Future input is weekly ending/count aggregates only, with at least 20 per published bucket. -->
  <section hidden id="weekly"><h2>Endings founders searched this week</h2></section>
  <section class="check-band" id="check-yours">
    <h2>Keep the name you want to say out loud</h2>
    <p>Start with your exact name on .com. If it’s taken, try .ai for an AI product, or say the .io version out loud. Compare those with a .com that adds a short word, like “get”.</p>
    <p class="check-help">Check what’s available and what your exact name costs to renew.</p>
    <div id="check">{{closingCheck}}</div>
  </section>
  </div>
  <section class="method"><div class="reading">
    <h2>How we counted</h2>
    <p>On {{day}}, we counted one listed site per startup across {{batches}} YC batches, from {{firstBatch}} through {{latest}}. Of {{eligible}} eligible companies, {{excluded}} had no usable site. A startup can change its domain after launch.</p>
    <details><summary>Coverage, sources and terms</summary>
      <p>We included public YC startups of any status with a listed location in a Bay Area town or city, or at Stanford. Each counted once. We left out fully remote companies and future batches.</p>
      <p>We took endings from the <a href="https://publicsuffix.org/list/">Public Suffix List</a> so endings like .co.uk stay together. We measured the name just before the ending. To match brands and prefixes, we kept letters and digits, ignored case and dropped spaces and punctuation. We kept legal suffixes such as Inc.</p>
      <p>For name shapes, <a href="https://www.nltk.org/howto/wordnet.html">WordNet</a> supplies English words. We split compounds at spaces, hyphens or capital letters, or into two words of at least three letters each. A single string of letters absent from the dictionary counts as “Possibly invented”. Other spellings go under “Other”.</p>
      <p>The sites come from <a href="https://github.com/yc-oss/api">YC OSS</a>, an unofficial feed of the <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/companies">YC directory</a>. YC’s <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/legal#tou">terms of use</a> restrict scraping and commercial reuse. The feed grants no separate data license. Domain Hound is independent of YC.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="funding-note"><summary>Funding sources and .com checks</summary>
      <p>We started with the 150 largest teams listed by YC and added companies with verified Form D filings. We included Emergent after checking its published round history. YC does not list its team size. Comparable revenue figures were unavailable.</p>
      <p>We added distinct public rounds and amounts sold in SEC filings. Corgi’s figure combines its named early rounds with three later filings. Its reported cumulative total differs from that sum. The table uses the six individual amounts.</p>
      <p>For each listed domain we checked its label with .com. “Yes” means the company listed that .com or it redirected to the listed site. “Registered only” means we confirmed registration without establishing a link to the company. Registration does not identify the owner.</p>
      <p><a href="{{leadSource}}">Emergent’s funding history</a> · <a href="https://www.greptile.com/blog/seed">Greptile’s seed round</a></p>
      <a href="/data/sf/top50.json" download>Download funding sources and domain checks (JSON)</a>
    </details>
    <div class="foot-links"><a href="/data/sf/endings.json" download>Download the counts (JSON)</a><button id="share" hidden>Share this page</button><span id="share-status" role="status"></span></div>
  </div></section>
  </article>
</main>
<footer><div class="frame"><a href="/">Domain Hound</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a><p>Not affiliated with Y Combinator. Data from YC's public directory.</p></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
